			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Reduce ApplicationState module to atomic placeholder\n\nStrip the verbose legacy documentation and complex re-export logic from `Source/ApplicationState/mod.rs` to align with the project's shift towards fine-grained, atomic state management.\n\nThe file is now reduced to a concise module header and declarations for `State`, `DTO`, and `Internal` sub-modules, with explicit `pub use` statements removed to enforce full path resolution (`State::ApplicationState::ApplicationState`) as established in recent refactors. The `non_snake_case` attribute is applied to the module file to suppress lints during this transitional period as consumers migrate to the new granular entry points.\n\nThis clears the namespace for the upcoming rewrite of the state layer while preserving the existing sub-module structure for future incremental implementation.",
